A||||3||Steve Normington||Aux Gage Box is Hot||||1||
Z||000000||Steve Normington||06-16-2001||01:12 AM||||How hot does the aux gage panel get? My car was in on w/o the engine running for much of the day and the panel housing was hot to the touch (not hot enough to burn, but very warm). Note: this is not OE, I wired them in myself as an add on, but the voltmeter and oil pressure are working. Could the volt and oil pressure warning lights cause this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-16-2001||10:36 AM||||Are the idiot lights on all the time?  If so, this is probably your problem.  If not, check something else.  Has it been sitting in the sun all day?  The top of the dash, top of the main gauge cluster and the aux gauges are the 1st to collect heat.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||06-16-2001||11:13 AM||||The idiot lights were on most of the time since the engine wasn't running. It was sitting in the sun, so that may have added to the problem. I just wanted to be sure that it wasn't a sign of impending doom.<P>Thanks for the info.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||06-16-2001||02:34 PM||||If the "Idiot Light" as you call them, were on all day, then yes, there is reason for it to get hot. I'm sure the sun greatly contributed to it being hot to the touch, feel the top of your dash, it should be just about as hot. I'm sure there is no reason to be concerned, unless somthing starts smelling like melted plastic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
